
How to Uninstall Oracle Database 11g on Windows 10
Step 1: Remove Oracle from Environment Variables
•	Right-click This PC → Properties
•	Click Advanced system settings
•	Click Environment Variables
•	Under System variables, double-click Path
•	Delete all Oracle-related entries
•	Click OK to save changes
Step 2: Remove Oracle Services from Registry
1.	Press Windows + S, type Run, and press Enter
2.	Type regedit → press Enter to open Registry Editor
3.	Navigate to: 
4.	HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE → SYSTEM → CurrentControlSet → Services
5.	Delete all Oracle-related service entries
Step 3: Remove Oracle Software from Registry
1.	In Registry Editor, go to: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE → SOFTWARE
2.	Delete all Oracle-related entries
Step 4: Restart Your Computer
•	Restart the PC to ensure all services are cleared
Step 5: Delete Oracle Setup Files
•	Navigate to the folder where Oracle was installed and delete it
Step 6: Delete Oracle from Program Files
1.	Open C:\Program Files
2.	Delete the Oracle folder
Step 7: Delete Oracle from Start Menu
•	Go to: C:\ProgramData\Microsoft\Windows\Start Menu\Programs
•	Delete any Oracle-related folders
✅ Note: After completing all steps, Oracle Database 11g will be completely removed from your Windows 10 system.
